{"nodes": [{"id": "drive_the_method_materials_expansion_mc54_seed_of_lambda", "label": "seed(\u039b) \u2014 the minimum generating set of a closed index", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/EXPANSION-MC54.md", "source_location": "D4", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Defined against the book's own \u211b taken verbatim from the sealed instrument, so the expansion measures the same operator the corpus ships rather than a re-implementation."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_expansion_mc54_t1_generation_criterion", "label": "T1 \u2014 the generation criterion (alphabet plus envelope agreement)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/EXPANSION-MC54.md", "source_location": "T1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "X\u2080 generates \u039b iff it reproduces every alphabet value and every envelope value; this is what licenses the set-cover formulation (elements = alphabet slots \u222a envelope steps) and was validated on 200/200 exact covers closing to 976."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_expansion_mc54_t2_alphabet_law", "label": "T2 \u2014 the alphabet law (every seed witnesses every alphabet value)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/EXPANSION-MC54.md", "source_location": "T2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cap-independent, because the proof uses only D1\u2013D4 and never a cap; the bit-reading corollary is that every column receives both a 0 and a 1 across any seed."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_expansion_mc54_t3_envelope_step_law", "label": "T3 \u2014 the envelope-step law", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/EXPANSION-MC54.md", "source_location": "T3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Equality at steps propagates to the whole alphabet because the running max is constant between steps; register 603's six channel conditions are the \u2113 \u2264 1 face of this law, and s\u2192s is not a step and was never forced."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_expansion_mc54_p4_non_uniqueness", "label": "P4 \u2014 non-uniqueness of the minimum seed, located as a Krein\u2013Milman failure", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/EXPANSION-MC54.md", "source_location": "P4", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "\u039b\u2088 has NO extreme points yet seed = 7, a maximal failure of the combinatorial Krein\u2013Milman property, which is exactly what permits 24,585 minimum generating sets. The seed's invariant content is T2 + T3 \u2014 alphabet slots and envelope steps \u2014 not cell identities."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_expansion_mc54_forced_set_chvatal", "label": "The forced set of the derived cover instance (Chv\u00e1tal reduction)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/EXPANSION-MC54.md", "source_location": "P4", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "What is common to all minimum covers is not an extreme point but a forced set \u2014 at \u039b\u2088 exactly one cell, (2,1,3,3,2,1,3,0) \u2014 and that forcing is cap-specific."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_expansion_mc54_edelman_jamison", "label": "Edelman & Jamison \u2014 anti-exchange closures and convex geometries", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/EXPANSION-MC54.md", "source_location": "PRIOR ART", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Named as NEW prior art for P4's negative content; the expansion claims no novelty for cited machinery, only for measuring the forced content of an index's minimum seeds across caps."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_expansion_mc54_closure_r_sealed", "label": "\u211b, the sealed closure instrument (D3)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/EXPANSION-MC54.md", "source_location": "D3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "drive_the_method_materials_expansion_mc54_t1_generation_criterion", "target": "drive_the_method_materials_expansion_mc54_seed_of_lambda", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/EXPANSION-MC54.md", "source_location": "T1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "drive_the_method_materials_expansion_mc54_t2_alphabet_law", "target": "drive_the_method_materials_expansion_mc54_t1_generation_criterion", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/EXPANSION-MC54.md", "source_location": "T2", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "drive_the_method_materials_expansion_mc54_t3_envelope_step_law", "target": "drive_the_method_materials_expansion_mc54_t1_generation_criterion", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/EXPANSION-MC54.md", "source_location": "T3", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "drive_the_method_materials_expansion_mc54_p4_non_uniqueness", "target": "drive_the_method_materials_expansion_mc54_edelman_jamison", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/EXPANSION-MC54.md", "source_location": "P4; PRIOR ART", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "drive_the_method_materials_expansion_mc54_p4_non_uniqueness", "target": "drive_the_method_materials_expansion_mc54_forced_set_chvatal", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/EXPANSION-MC54.md", "source_location": "P4", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "drive_the_method_materia